# 9. ElastiCache / Redis

Pour la fraude temps réel, c'est particulièrement intéressant.

Architecture :

```text
Transaction
     ↓
Fraud API
     ↓
Redis
     ↓
Features
```

Exemple :

```text
transactions_last_10min = 7
amount_last_1h = 850 €
unique_devices_24h = 3
```

---

# 10. Question d'entretien

> **Why wouldn't you calculate these features directly from PostgreSQL?**

### Réponse

> Because querying and aggregating large amounts of transactional data synchronously for every request could introduce significant latency and create a bottleneck. I would precompute or incrementally maintain frequently used real-time features and store them in a low-latency system such as Redis.

